# URLs lychee must not check. Each line is a regex (or glob) matched against
# the extracted link. Keep every entry narrow enough that it can only match the
# one link it was written for -- a broad pattern here silently hides real rot.

# Not a link: lychee's plain-text extractor reads the cosign
# --certificate-identity-regexp documented in .goreleaser.yml's comment block
# and stops at the regex's backslash, turning '^https://github\.com/...' into
# the hostname 'github'. The identical string in README.md and SECURITY.md is
# not reported, because there it sits in a fenced block the markdown extractor
# skips. Nothing to fix in the comment: the regex is correct as written and has
# to stay copy-pasteable.
^https://github/$

# Correct as written, and 404 by design. This is the GitHub Actions OIDC issuer
# *identifier* passed to `cosign verify-blob --certificate-oidc-issuer`, not a
# page. The issuer serves its metadata at /.well-known/openid-configuration and
# returns 404 on the root path, so a reachability check can never pass. Matched
# exactly so a genuinely broken githubusercontent link still reports.
^https://token\.actions\.githubusercontent\.com/?$

# A Task template, not a URL. .taskfiles/dev.yml interpolates
# {{.GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION}} into the golangci-lint install-script path at run
# time; lychee sees the literal braces, percent-encodes them, and 404s on the
# unresolved path. Anchored on the template marker so the same URL with a real
# version tag substituted in is still checked.
^https://raw\.githubusercontent\.com/golangci/golangci-lint/(%7B%7B|\{\{)\.
